            "title": "Trump's plans for Venezuelan oil, defense spending hikes",
            "description": "<p>President Trump is giving Wall Street investors whiplash with a deluge of new policy proposals, from hiking defense spending to $1.5 trillion to expecting 50 million barrels of Venezuelan oil (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/CL=F\">CL=F</a>, <a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/BZ=F\">BZ=F</a>) and plans to <a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/news/blackstone-stock-sinks-after-trump-plans-steps-to-ban-institutional-investors-from-buying-single-family-homes-184525826.html\">ban institutional investors</a> from buying single-family homes.</p>\n<p>Yahoo Finance Washington correspondent <a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://www.yahoo.com/author/ben-werschkul/\">Ben Werschkul</a> comes on the program to explain Trump's vision for the US occupation of Venezuela in relation to the oil industry, while the administration seeks to raise its defense budget in 2027.</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more\u00a0<a data-i13n=\"cpos:5;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/morning-brief/\">Morning Brief</a>.</p>",
